1
00:03:57,777 --> 00:04:03,777
Witness the beginning of evil.

2
00:07:55,555 --> 00:08:01,555
Resident Evil: Welcome to Raccoon City is a action, horror,
science fiction film directed by Johannes Roberts.

3
00:11:53,333 --> 00:11:59,333
Once the booming home of pharmaceutical giant Umbrella
Corporation, Raccoon City is now a dying Midwestern town.

4
00:15:51,111 --> 00:15:57,111
The company’s exodus left the city a wasteland…with
great evil brewing below the surface.

5
00:19:48,888 --> 00:19:54,888
When that evil is unleashed, the townspeople are forever…changed…and a small group of survivors must
work together to uncover the truth behind Umbrella and make it through the night.

6
00:23:46,666 --> 00:23:52,666
Claire Redfield, played by Kaya Scodelario.

7
00:27:44,444 --> 00:27:50,444
Jill Valentine, played by Hannah John-Kamen.

8
00:31:42,222 --> 00:31:48,222
Chris Redfield, played by Robbie Amell.

9
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:46,000
Albert Wesker, played by Tom Hopper.

10
00:39:37,777 --> 00:39:43,777
Leon Kennedy, played by Avan Jogia.

11
00:43:35,555 --> 00:43:41,555
Chief Irons, played by Donal Logue.

12
00:47:33,333 --> 00:47:39,333
Resident Evil: Welcome to Raccoon City is a 2021 action horror film based on the Resident Evil video game series by
Capcom, and serves as a reboot and the seventh live-action film of the Resident Evil film series.

13
00:51:31,111 --> 00:51:37,111
Written and directed by Johannes Roberts, the film stars Kaya Scodelario, Hannah
John-Kamen, Robbie Amell, Tom Hopper, Avan Jogia, Donal Logue, and Neal McDonough.

14
00:55:28,888 --> 00:55:34,888
Set in 1998, and primarily adapting the first and second games, it follows a
group of survivors during a zombie outbreak in Raccoon City.

15
00:59:26,666 --> 00:59:32,666
It is the first live-action film in the series not to feature Milla
Jovovich in the lead role of her character Alice.

16
01:03:24,444 --> 01:03:30,444
Development took place in early 2017, after Resident Evil: The Final Chapter was
released, with producer James Wan expressing interest in the project.

17
01:07:22,222 --> 01:07:28,222
Later, Constantin Film chairman Martin Moszkowicz said that a
reboot of the film series was in development.

18
01:11:20,000 --> 01:11:26,000
In the same month, Wan was called to produce the reboot with a script by Greg Russo; subsequently,
Roberts was hired as both writer and director and both Wan and Russo left the project.

19
01:15:17,777 --> 01:15:23,777
Filming began on October 17, 2020, in Greater Sudbury, Ontario, Canada.

20
01:19:15,555 --> 01:19:21,555
The film underwent reshoots in May 2021.

21
01:23:13,333 --> 01:23:19,333
Resident Evil: Welcome to Raccoon City had its world premiere at the Grand Rex in Paris on November 19, 2021, and
was theatrically released on November 24, 2021, in the United States by Sony Pictures Releasing.

22
01:27:11,111 --> 01:27:17,111
The film grossed $42 million worldwide and received mixed reviews from critics, who
praised its faithfulness to the first two games, but criticized its writing.

23
01:31:08,888 --> 01:31:14,888
A sequel was planned but cancelled due to the film's commercial failure.

24
01:35:06,666 --> 01:35:12,666
Another reboot is slated to be released on September 18, 2026.

25
01:39:04,444 --> 01:39:10,444
The film explores themes of biological weapon,
orphanage, dystopia, mutant, infection.

26
01:43:02,222 --> 01:43:08,222
The tone is dark and thought_provoking.
